=== HAS A LIVE LINK (the link is in LINKS, above) ===

fsd/
  -> the specification, the requirements source of truth
  -> versioning: "{{title}} - Functional Specifications - V<n>.pdf", never overwritten. Build from the
     highest number (compared as numbers: V9 is below V15).

permissions-matrix/
  -> the source for permissions where the specification is silent
  -> versioning: same V<n> scheme as fsd/

product-questions-and-answers/
  -> answers the product team gave outside the specification proper
  -> versioning: same V<n> scheme as fsd/

qa-artifacts/
  -> QA's own test cases and checklists - corroborating evidence, not a requirement source
  -> versioning: the superseded copy moves into backup/ with a date suffix; the new one takes the
     plain filename.

fe-integration-bugs/
  -> the front-end team's integration findings
  -> versioning: as qa-artifacts/

release-plan/
  -> the client's release plan
  -> versioning: as qa-artifacts/

wireframes/ (wireframes-V1/, wireframes-V2/, ...)
  -> screen designs, informing but not overriding the specification
  -> versioning: export the changed frames into the next wireframes-V<n>/ folder.

client-documents/
  -> documents the client delivered alongside the specification - background evidence
  -> versioning: each file under its delivered name; a newer copy gets a "- V<n>" suffix.

=== NO LIVE LINK ===

(A source delivered as files, with nothing to fetch or diff. Its folder needs no read-me.txt: this
entry is its record. An FSD delivered as a file also keeps its LINKS line, as "none - delivered as a file".)

fe-api-contracts/
  -> the front end's request for endpoints, as delivered.

email-templates/
  -> email designs as delivered.
